('Trichoscopy: A Text and Atlas', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/e41bee04c_190966.jpg', 'Dr. Subrota Malakar', 'Jaypee Brothers Medical Publisher (India)', 'Dermatology', '9789386150745', 'English', 385, '1st Edition, 2017', 13230.0, 6952, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'A Text and Atlas Salient Features The first book to demonstrate and decode the language of trichoscopy with illustrations Methodical demonstration of trichoscopic findings in hair disorders aids in understanding the subject Self-assessment images serve as an invaluable tool to judge the hold on the subject after a thorough reading Algorithms listed at the end of the book help in approaching any hair disorder in clinical practice with ease Demonstration of multiple new signs and findings arouses the inquisitiveness and interest of the readers. Show More'),
('Essentials of Medicine for Dental Students', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Essentials_of_Medicine_for_Dental_Studen-K_Anil_Tripathi-bb55a-189031.jpg', 'K Anil Tripathi , K Kamal Sawlani', 'Jaypee Brothers Medical Publisher (India)', 'Dental', '9789354651267', 'English', 343, '4th Edition, 2022', 1710.0, 1049, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'Essentials of Medicine for Dental Students Salient Features • The contents of he book are in accordance with the BDS curriculum as per Dental Council of India. . The text is simple, clear, and concise and illustrated with the help of figures and tables. Many more has been added in the new edition to make the subject more comprehensible. . The information provided is latest and is according to National/International guidelines where applicable. Recently introduced drugs have been mentioned in the text, particularly those in regard to diabetes mellitus, HIV, Hepatitis C, blood cancers, and tuberculosis. • Tips are given at the end of each chapter explaining the importance and implication of knowledge in real practice. • A section is dedicated to the ongoing Pandemic due to COVID 19. •Multiple Choice Questions and Fill in the Blanks are given in each chapter for Self Assessment. Show More'),
('Review of Medical Microbiology and Immunology', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Review_of_Medical_Microbiology_and_Immun-Warren_E_Levinson-c857f-252006.jpg', 'Warren E. Levinson', 'McGraw Hill India', 'Microbiology', '9781260469424', 'English', 864, '16th Edition, 2020', 3958.0, 3147, '65% Off', NULL, NULL, 'In Stock', 'Some parts of the book SHAPE and SIZE OF BACTERIA Bacteria are classified by shape into three basic groups: cocci, bacilli, and spirochetes (Figure 2-1). The cocci are round, the bacilli are rods, and the spirochetes are spiral-shaped. Some bacteria are variable in shape and are said to be pleomorphic (heterogeneous shape). The shape of a bacterium is determined by its rigid cell wall. The microscopic appearance of a bacterium is one of the most important criteria used in its identification. In addition to their characteristic shapes, the arrangement of bacteria is important. For example, certain cocci occur in pairs (diplococci), some in chains (streptococci), and others in grapelike clusters (staphylococci). These arrangements are determined by the orientation and degree of attachment of the bacteria at the time of cell division. The arrangement of rods and spirochetes is medically less important and is not described in this introductory chapter. Bacteria range in size from about 0.2 to 5 um (Figure 2-2). The smallest bacteria (Mycoplasma) are about the same size as the largest viruses (poxviruses) and are the smallest organisms capable of existing outside a host. The longest bacteria are the size of some yeasts and human red blood cells (7 μm). Show More'),
('Illustrated Textbook Of Pediatrics', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Illustrated_Textbook_Of_Pediatrics-Shakur_Md_Salim-39dc3-237213.jpg', 'Dr. Md. Salim Shakur', 'Jaypee Brothers Medical Publisher (India)', 'Pediatrics', '9789351525158', 'English', 987, '2nd Edition, 1 January 2015', 3771.0, 2172, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'CONTENTS 1. Neonatology 2. Clinical Genetics 3. Fluid and Electrolyte Balance and its Disorders 4. Acid-Base Balance and Disturbance 5. Growth and Development 6. Nutrition and its Disorders 7. Gastroenterology 8. Hepatology 9. Structure of the Respiratory Tree (Applied Anatomy) 10. Integrated Management of Childhood Illness 11. Cardiac Disorders 12. Pediatric Neurology 13. Child Abuse and Child Protection 14. Infectious Diseases 15. Endocrinology 16. Nephrology 17. Hemato-oncologic Disorder 18. Pediatric Dermatology 19. Joint and Bone Disorders 20. Drug Overdoses and Poisoning 21. Procedures 22. Drug Therapy in Children 23. Chart Show More'),
('Applied English Grammar And Composition (For High Schools)', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/f9134bf8a_126629.jpg', 'P C Das', 'New Central Book Agency (India)', NULL, '9788173816505', 'English', 724, 'Reprint, 2022', 1100.0, 935, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', '"অ্যাপ্লাইড ইংলিশ গ্রামার অ্যান্ড কম্পোজিশন" বইটির সম্পর্কে কিছু কথাঃ অ্যাপ্লাইড ইংলিশ গ্রামার অ্যান্ড কম্পোজিশন বইটি নবম-দশম শ্রেনীর ইংরেজী শেখার জন্য একটি গুরুত্বপূর্ন বই। বইটিতে ইংরেজীর অনেক জটিল বিষয়গুলো অনেক সহজ করে ব্যাখ্যা করা হয়েছে। বইটি শিক্ষার্থীদের জন্য একটি সহায়ক বই। Show More'),
('Allen''s Keynotes and Characteristics with Comparisons', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Allens_Keynotes_and_Characteristics_with-HC_Allen-a9dae-253975.jpg', 'H.C. Allen', 'B.Jain Publishers (India)', NULL, '9788131901243', 'English', 402, NULL, 436.0, 414, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'In homeopathy, a comparison of the pathogenesis of a remedy with the registered anamnesis of the patient is of utmost important; he must distinguish the apparently similar symptoms of two or more medicines to reach the similliumum. In order for the student or practitioner to be able to do this correctly, the student must have the correct knowledge of the specificity of the remedy, something peculiar, unusual, or sufficiently characteristic in the polychrest remedy that can be used as a central point of comparison. This edition is popular due to its precision and comprehensiveness. No symptom is lost to the readers even on causal reading due to the special arrangement of symptoms. KEY FEATURES: The symptoms are unaltered in substance and the language remains unchanged. All abbreviations are standardized according to the Synthesis. A separate section for bowel nosodes provides a concise idea about them. Show More'),
('Forest History : International Studies on Socio-Economic and Forest Ecosystem Change 2', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/a309a0d88_60300.jpg', 'M Agnoletti', 'Cabi Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9780851994192', 'English', 418, '1st Edition, 2000', 17732.0, 9810, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'IUFRO Research Series The International Union of Forestry Research Organizations (IUFRO), with its 14,000 scientists from 700 member institutions in 100 countries, is organized into nearly 300 research units that annually hold approximately 60 confer- ences, workshops and other meetings. The individual papers, proceedings and other material arising from these units and meetings are often published but in a wide array of different journals and other publications. The object of the IUFRO Research Series is to offer a single, uniform outlet for high quality publications arising from major IUFRO meetings and other products of IUFRO''s research units. The editing, publishing and dissemination experience of CABI Publishing and the huge spread of scientific endeavours of IUFRO combine here to make information widely available that is of value to policy makers, resource managers, peer scientists and educators. The Executive Board of IUFRO forms the Editorial Advisory Board for the Series and provides the monitoring and uniformity that such a high quality series requires in addition to the editorial work of the conference organizers. While adding a new body of information to the plethora currently dealing with forestry and related resources, this series seeks to provide a single, uniform forum and style that all forest scientists will turn to first as an outlet for their conference material and other products, and that the users of information will also see as a reliable and reputable source. Although the official languages of IUFRO include English, French, German and Spanish, the majority of modern scientific papers are published in English. In this series, all books will be published in English as the main language, allowing papers occasionally to be in other languages. Show More'),
('Oxford Compact English-English-Hindi Dictionary', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Oxford_Compact_English_English_Hindi_Dic-_Abraham_Pais-f9778-341229.jpg', 'Abraham Pais', 'Oxford University Press (India)', 'Free Shipping', '9780199467082', 'English', 836, NULL, 799.0, 799, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'Contents Preface v-vi Guide to the dictionary vii-ix Dictionary quiz x-xi Phonetic symbols xii The Dictionary A-Z 1-799 . Study pages Contents 800-801 Prepositions of place 802 Prepositions of movement 803 Numbers 804-805 Time and dates 806 Telephoning 807 Words that go together 808-809 Health 810 Writing letters and emails 811-812 Filling in forms 813 Geographical names 814-818 2000 Keywords 819-830 Irregular verbs 831-832 Key to study pages 833-836 Show More'),
('Fake - MM Export Ed.', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Fake_MM_Export_Ed-Robert_T_Kiyosaki-ce999-344774.jpg', 'Robert T. Kiyosaki', 'Plata Publishing (India)', 'Free Shipping', '9781612681092', 'English', 560, '1st Edition, 2020', 1198.0, 822, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'INTRODUCTION THE FUTURE IS FAKE This book, Fake, was completed in April 2018—and being edited for release in the Fall of 2018. On May 28, 2018, I was walking past a newsstand, scanning rows and rows of magazines that were calling out, "Look at me!" "Pick me up!" "Buy me!" "Read me!" Obviously, the magazines with pretty women and fast cars on the covers spoke to me the most loudly. Yet, it was a rather bland cover of Time magazine that grabbed me by the collar and said, You must read me. The headline on the cover shouted: How My Generation Broke America That magazine article—and the impact it had on me-delayed the publication of this book. Show More'),
('More Magic of the Minimum Dose', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/More_Magic_of_the_Minimum_Dose-Dorothy_Shepherd-3af1b-254708.jpg', 'Dorothy Shepherd', 'B.Jain Publishers (India)', 'Medicine', '9788131948514', 'English', 286, '1st Edition, 2017', 498.0, 411, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'CONTENTS 1. SOME INTRODUCTORY REMARKS 2.THE BENEFITS OF HOMOEOPATHY 3.ANIMAL RESPONSE TO HOMOEOPATHIC REMEDIES 4.RESPIRATORY DISEASES 5.COLDS AND CHILLS ... 6.SOME ACUTE CONDITIONS 7.THE VALUE OF ACONITE 8.ABDOMINAL UPSETS OF EVERYDAY LIFE 9.TWO OUT-PATIENT CASES 10. LACHESIS IN WOMEN''S DISEASES .. 11. CONSIDER HOMOEOPATHY BEFORE SURGERY 12. TUMOUR OF THE BREAST 13. TWO CARDIAC CASES 14. BOILS AND CARBUNCLES 15. REMEDIES OF FEAR AND STRESS 16. A CASE OF SEVERE EYE AFFECTION 17.HOMOEOPATHY IN SKIN DISEASES 18. SOME COMPLICATIONS OF INFECTIOUS DISEASES 19. IMMUNIZATION .... 20. ON THE PREVENTION OF DISEASE 21. DIPHTHERIA AND ITS NOSODE 22. ENEURISIS OR BED-WETTING 23. EAR DISCHARGE 24. MORBILLINUM (MEASLES SERUM) 25. SCARLATINUM (SCARLET FEVER SERUM) 26. MENTAL DISEASE AND HOMOEOPATHY 27. NERVOUS DISORDERS 28. WHAT IS CURABLE IN MEDICINE 29. WHAT IS CURATIVE IN MEDICINE Glossary of Medical Show More'),
('Rapid Prescribing', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Rapid_Prescribing_Using_Peculiar_Symptom-Dr_Muhammed_Rafeeque_-41ea2-254349.jpg', 'Dr. Muhammed Rafeeque', 'B. Jain Regular (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Health, family, recipe, fashion', '9788131908389', 'English', 135, '1st Edition, 2008', 290.0, 240, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'A much needed book which includes rare remedies in Homoeopathic practice are described under two sections with some illustrations. A great compilation of peculiar symptoms of homoeopathic drugs which one can never find at one place. The work of different stalwarts of homoeopathy is also expressed in many drugs during their clinical practice and their observation. Physicians have shared their clinical experience in almost every drug with potency selection and administration of doses. This book proves the best key in understanding and giving more stress on the special symptoms of the drugs. One of the very commonly used approaches is the preion on the basis of characteristic symptoms or uncommon symptoms. Uncommon symptoms are those that are found in few people and few medicines. They are usually characteristic because they aid in individualization. But sometimes it happens that there is a strong peculiar symptom with just one or two medicines listed against it in the repertory. Such a symptom can be a sensation, location, causative factor, modality or concomitant. When such a strong uncommon symptom is found, homeopaths often make a preion just on the basis of that particular symptom. This book tries to list all such uncommon symptoms that are present in just one or two medicines and thus have a high specific value. The symptoms are arranged in the following order: Mind, Sensations, Causation, Modalities, Concomitants and Miscellaneous. Certainly a step to help rise higher up the level of accuracy in practice. Key Features:- Gives light to the general symptoms but gives more emphasis on the special symptomatology. Pathogenic effects of large and small doses. The book lists 3333 uncommon symptoms. A sure shot guide to keynote prescribing. Show More'),
('Decachords Top Ten Indications of 120 Homeopathic Remedies', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Decachords_Top_Ten_Indications_of_120_Ho-John_H_Clarke-44bab-254044.jpg', 'John H. Clarke', 'B. Jain Regular (India)', 'Homeopathic', '9788131907610', 'English', 146, NULL, 250.0, 207, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'A collection of the most commonly used remedies with some necessary clues to their prescribing, this book is a pocket memoir of about 50 homeopathic medicines. Additional remedies included at the end of the book as Pentachords, make the total number of books 120. Inclusions from the works of Sir John Weir and Dr. Wheeler and from those of Dr. Allen, Cowperthwaite, and Nash enrich the book further. Key Features:- Abbreviations and names of drugs have been standardized according to Synthesis. Improved and more readable fonts have been introduced with increased font size. General hints pertaining to the indications of each remedy have been incorporated. The hierarchy of symptoms has been followed in the order- Generals, Mentals, Peculiars, and Particulars- which makes it easy for a student to understand the drug. Show More'),
('Managing Tourism and Hospitality Services', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Managing_Tourism_and_Hospitality_Service-Eric_Laws-8d9da-228039.jpg', NULL, 'Cabi Publishing (India)', 'Free Shipping', '9781845930127', 'English', 338, 'Edition, 2006', 17487.0, 17487, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'In Stock', 'The Structure of this Book Managing Tourism and Hospitality Services is organized in six parts. The 28 chapters deal with a wide range of issues, providing analyses of international tourism and hospitality man- agement practices from many sectors of the industry, and utilizing an interesting selection of research methodologies and conceptual approaches. As the editors show in detail in the review and synthesis of the concluding chapter of this book, the work presented here makes a substantial contribution to the better understanding of current tourism and hospital- ity management and emergent research capabilities, while identifying some gaps and the need for further research in the future. Part I deals with the core issue for tourism and hospitality managers of customer satisfac- tion. The five chapters examine some specific examples and draw together a range of theo- retical and methodological approaches to customer satisfaction research and manage- ment. This theme of customer satisfaction is taken up in many of the subsequent chapters in this book. Show More'),
('The Essence Of Materia Medica: 2nd Edition', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Essence_Of_Materia_Medica_2nd_Editio-George_Vithoulkas-4ac9d-253985.jpg', 'George Vithoulkas', 'B. Jain Regular (India)', 'Others Medical Book', '9788131902011', 'English', 218, '2nd Edition, 2009', 476.0, 476, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '"The Essence of Materia Medica" by George Vithoulkas is a comprehensive guide to homeopathic remedies, providing an in-depth understanding of the key remedies in homeopathic practice. The book is based on Vithoulkas'' vast clinical experience and is intended for homeopathic practitioners and students who wish to gain deeper insights into the essential characteristics of various remedies. The focus of the book is to capture the "essence" of each homeopathic remedy. Instead of presenting a detailed list of symptoms, Vithoulkas distills the remedies into their core psychological, emotional, and physical patterns. This approach helps practitioners more easily match remedies to patients based on their overall state, not just isolated symptoms. Key features of the book include: Clear Deions of Remedies: Vithoulkas emphasizes the core nature of each remedy, focusing on its emotional and psychological effects as well as its physical symptoms. This helps practitioners understand how a remedy resonates with a patient''s personality and general disposition. Differentiation between Similar Remedies: Many remedies in homeopathy have overlapping symptoms, which can make it difficult to choose the right one. Vithoulkas offers valuable guidance on distinguishing between similar remedies by highlighting their subtle differences. Practical Insights: The book is filled with practical advice based on real-life cases. Vithoulkas shares his experience of how certain remedies behave in clinical practice, offering tips on how to recognize the correct remedy and how patients are likely to respond to treatment. Focused Approach: By concentrating on the core essence of each remedy, the book helps practitioners cut through the complexity of Materia Medica and homeopathic repertories. This makes it easier to identify the correct remedy in practice. "The Essence of Materia Medica" is widely regarded as a valuable tool for homeopaths who want to deepen their understanding of remedies beyond superficial symptoms. Vithoulkas'' insights offer a more intuitive and holistic view of homeopathic medicine, making it easier to select the most appropriate remedy for each patient based on their overall constitution and mental state. Overall, the book serves as an essential resource for anyone practicing or studying homeopathy, providing a concise yet profound understanding of the remedies and their therapeutic applications. Show More'),
('Periodic Table', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Periodic_Table-DK_Publishing-183df-352242.jpg', 'DK Publishing', 'DK Children (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9780241413029', 'English', 160, 'Edition, 2020', 798.0, 798, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'A brand new science book for kids joins this hugely successful mini-encyclopedia series that packs a whole lot of information into your pocket. Discover all the major elements of the periodic table, arranged in chapters according to their group, including alkaline earth metals, lanthanides, and noble gases. Every important element - from hydrogen via carbon, oxygen, and gold to oganesson (that''s element number 118) - is presented here. Each element is featured in its own catalogue-style entry, with a photo of the element in its raw state or in use; a caption explaining important information ranging from where it''s found to its main uses; and a fact list presenting the key data, including the date of discovery and all atomic information as found on the periodic table. Plus there are stunning full-page photos showing elements as you have never seen them before - perhaps inside machinery that you can''t normally delve into; or in stunning macro photography that reveals microscopic details invisible to the human eye. The style of the Pocket Eyewitness series is perfect for all children, from reluctant readers who can easily digest the key points through to budding Marie Curies and Louis Pasteurs who want to know more about the most essential particles on the planet. Show More'),
