('Arihant 49 Years JEE Advanced (1978–2026) and 25 Years JEE Main (2002–2026) Mathematics PYQ Book', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Arihant_49_Years_JEE_Advanced_19782026_a-Amit_M_Agarwal-653bd-481205.jpg', 'Amit M Agarwal', 'Arihant Publications (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9789378169922', 'English', 888, 'Edition , 2026', 1790.0, 1611, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '49 Years JEE Advanced 25 Years JEE Main Mathematics is a highly structured, comprehensive archive of previous years'' questions designed for engineering aspirants aiming for India''s premier institutes. Serving as a complete practice and revision system, this book goes beyond standard question banks to help students bridge the gap between fundamental concepts and actual exam-level problem-solving. Who Can Benefit Engineering aspirants preparing for JEE Main and JEE Advanced examinations. Candidates looking to master Mathematics through a highly structured, level-wise, and chapter-wise approach. Students seeking to analyze changing exam trends, weightage, and high-frequency question patterns over the last several decades. Book Deion Arihant''s Chapterwise-Topicwise-Levelwise Solved Papers provide an extensively compiled repository of past examination questions for both JEE Main and Advanced. It acts as a systematic preparation tool to reinforce learning, eradicate conceptual weaknesses, and build a flawless strategy for the final exam. Dual-Exam Coverage: Features 49 Years of JEE Advanced (2026-1978) and 25 Years of JEE Main (2026-2002) past questions. Deep Organization: Categorized carefully into a chapter-wise, topic-wise, and level-wise framework for targeted preparation. Not Just PYQs: Upgraded with high-yield assessment indicators to transform regular practice into a dynamic revision system. Guaranteed Clarity: Equipped with detailed, accurate, and step-by-step solutions written by expert faculty to ensure complete conceptual understanding. What Sets This Book Apart Weightage Indicator: Built-in analysis metrics that highlight the distribution and importance of different chapters and topics over the years. 3-Level Practice Blueprint: Systematically arranged questions that elevate an aspirant’s skills progressively from foundational application to advanced problem-solving. High Frequency Show More'),
('How I Raised Myself from Failure to Success in Selling', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/43ed3850ca84_135166.jpg', 'Frank Bettger', 'Simon & Schuster (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9780671794378', 'English', 191, '1st Edition,1992', 798.0, 798, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Some parts of the book This Idea Put Me Back Into Selling After I Had Quit . Looking across years, I am astou, I am astounded how trivialities have changed the entire coursse of my life. As I have already said, after ten miserable, disheartening months trying to sell life insurance, I gave up all hope of ever being able to sell anything. I resigned, and I spent several days answering want ads. I wanted a job as a shipping clerk, because as a boy I had worked for the American Radiator Company, hammering nails into crates and stencilling them for shipment. With my limited education, I thought I could qualify for that kind of work. But try as I did, I couldn''t even get a job as a shipping clerk. I was not only discouraged; I was in the depths of despair. I fig- ured that I''d have to go back to riding my bicycle and collecting installments for George Kelly''s. My highest hope was to get my old job back at $18 a week. Show More'),
('Case History and Data Interpretation in Medical Practice (3rd Edition)', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/bc8db49da_55254.jpg', 'A.B.M. Abdullah', 'Jaypee Brothers Medical Publisher (India)', 'Medicine', '9789351523758', 'English', 504, '3rd Edition, 2015', 2990.0, 2990, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Design and Analysis of Algorithms', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/44c95112e_160041.jpg', 'S Sridhar', 'Oxford University Press (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9780198093695', 'English', 788, '1st edition, 2014', 1900.0, 1900, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'DESIGN AND ANALYSIS OF ALGORITHMS Design and Analysis of Algorithms is designed to serve as a textbook for the undergraduate students of computer science engineering and information technology as well as postgraduate students of computer applications. The book aims to empower students with in-depth knowledge of the fundamental concepts and the design, analysis, and implementation aspects of algorithms. The book begins with the basics of algorithms and problem-solving concepts followed by an introduction to algorithm writing, and analysis of iterative and recursive algorithms. In-depth explanations and designing techniques of various types of algorithms used for problem-solving such as brute force technique, divide-and-conquer technique, decrease-and- conquer strategy, greedy approach, transform-and-conquer strategy, dynamic programming, branch-and-bound approach, and backtracking are provided in the book. It also covers discussion of string algorithms, iterative improvement, linear programming, computability theory, NP-hard problems, NP-completeness, randomized algorithms, approximation algorithms, and parallel algorithms. The book includes a variety of chapter-end pedagogical features such as point-wise summary, glossary, review questions, exercises, and additional problems to help readers test their understanding and also apply and practise the concepts learnt. Appendices on basic mathematics and proof techniques are given to aid students refresh the fundamental concepts. . Key Features ■ In-depth treatment for topics such as greedy approach, dynamic programming, transform-and-conquer technique, decrease-and-conquer technique, linear programming, and randomized and approximation algorithms ■ Dedicated chapters on backtracking and branch-and-bound techniques, string matching algorithms, and parallel algorithms ■ Extensive discussion on the developing and designing aspects of algorithms using minimal mathematics and numerous examples ■ Judicious presentation of algorithms using step-wise approach throughout the text Historical notes on various topics and chapter-end crossword puzzles provided to engage readers and enhance their interest in the subject Show More'),
('Handbook For Orthopaedics Examination Theory and Practical', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Handbook_For_Orthopaedics_Examination_Th-Kaushik_Banarji_-8dfb9-251545.jpg', 'Kaushik Banarji', 'Academic Publishers (Indian)', NULL, '9789387162204', 'English', 304, '7th Edition, 1 January 2018', 1450.0, 1450, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Some parts of the book What is your diagnosis? This is a case of R/L sided; unilateral/bilat- eral; untreated/neglected/incompletely treated relapsed; idiopathic; mild-mobile/severe-rigid variety (Pirani score for PG students) of congenital talipes equinovarus deformity, in a month old boy/girl. [Always search for signs of syndromic vari- ety and other congenital abnormalities, and include them in your diagnosis when found e.g., development dysplasia hip (page 290), spina bifida (page 269), congenital radio-ulnar synos- tosis (page 188), constriction rings, etc.] What does talipes mean? Tali i.e., talus (ankle in Latin), Pes i.e., foot. Literally Talar foot, figuratively → walking on talus; practically meaning any. deformity of foot around talus. Show More'),
