('Textbook of Pharmacology', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Textbook_of_Pharmacology-F_S_K_Barar_-e895b-332400.jpg', 'F. S. K. Barar', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Medical', '9788121940801', 'English', 571, 'Reprint, 2022', 1798.0, 1798, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Textbook of Pharmacology is a collection of fundamental concepts of the subjects, aiming at the safe and effective use of drugs in the treatment of disease. Show More'),
('Oxford Handbook of Clinical Medicine', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/fc15adf95_192173.jpg', 'Longmore Wilkson Baldwin', 'Oxford University Press (India)', 'Medicine', '9780198729884', 'English', 864, '9th edition, 2014', 2798.0, 2798, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Letters from a Stoic', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/b61ffcf3a_170074.jpg', 'Lucius Seneca', 'CreateSpace Independent Publishing Platform (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9781539377047', 'English', 318, 'First Edition, 2016', 3198.0, 3198, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Some parts of the book I. On Saving Time Greetings from Seneca to his friend Lucilius. Continue to act thus, my dear Lucilius - set yourself free for your own sake; gather and save your time, which till lately has been forced from you, or filched away, or has merely slipped from your hands. Make yourself believe the truth of my words, that certain moments are tom from us, that some are gently removed, and that others glide beyond our reach. The most disgraceful kind of loss, however, is that due to carelessness. Furthermore, if you will pay close heed to the problem, you will find that the largest portion of our life passes while we are doing ill, a goodly share while we are doing nothing, and the whole while we are doing that which is not to the purpose. 2. What man can you show me who places any value on his time, who reckons the worth of each day, who understands that he is dying daily? For we are mistaken when we look forward to death; the major portion of death has already passed. Whatever years be behind us are in death''s hands. Show More'),
('Practical Pharmaceutical In-organic Chemistry', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/41c972d58_185844.jpg', 'Bayya Subba , V Alagarsamy Rao', 'Pharma Med Press', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9789352301942', 'English', 249, '2nd Edition, 2019', 798.0, 798, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'The book is unique of its kind in giving clear understanding of the various experiments of pharmaceutical in-organic chemistry for undergraduate students. The experiments in the book are planned to suit all Indian Universities syllabi at the level of D. Pharm., B. Pharm., Pharm D. (Post- Baccalaureate of Pharmacy) and Pharm. D. The book is written considering all latest official standard procedures. . Features • Most important feature of the book is its self-explanatory presentation. Special concentration is made on giving clear details of limit test for lead for easy understanding. Every chemical reagent used in the experiment is explained for its purpose, a highlight in the book. Experiments relating to assays were designed taking into consideration of all types of assays. • Identification tests of anions and cations were presented lucidly for easy memory by the students. • Semi-micro analysis is new for even teachers in some of the universities. A detailed lay out and necessary information is included. • A proper exposure of the student in handling viva-voce is necessary and all the possible questions are included. . Appended Features • Additional Experiments under every Category Emphasized on specific test for purity of certain in-organic drugs. Compiled list of Assay methods of Small Molecule Drugs as per Indian Pharmacopoeia-2014 and Addendum-2015. Show More'),
('Capital Volume I', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/rokimg_20151018_105540.gif', 'Karl Marx', 'Penguin Classics (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9780140445688', 'English', 1141, 'Reprint, 1990', 1998.0, 1998, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '''A groundbreaking work of economic analysis. It is also a literary masterpice'' Francis Wheen, GuardianOne of the most notorious and influential works of modern times, Capital is an incisive critique of private property and the social relations it generates. Living in exile in England, where this work was largely written, Marx drew on a wide-ranging knowledge of its society to support his analysis. Arguing that capitalism would cause an ever-increasing division in wealth and welfare, he predicted its abolition and replacement by a system with common ownership of the means of production. Capital rapidly acquired readership throughout the world, to become a work described by Marx''s collaborator Friedrich Engels as ''the Bible of the working class''.Translated by BEN FOWKES with an Introduction by ERNEST MANDEL Show More'),
('Crop Breeding and Biotechnology', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Crop_Breeding_and_Biotechnology_-Hari_Har_Ram-f34d5-256441.jpg', 'Hari Har Ram', 'Kalyani Publishers (India)', 'Agriculture', '9789353592332', 'English', 747, 'Reprinted, 2025', 1598.0, 1598, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'The second edition of the book entitled ''Crop Breeding and Biotechnology presents the application of breeding and biotechnology to improvement of major field crops particularly in context of India. Crop-wise individual chapters deal with origin, distribution, brief botanical deion, pollination, breeding objectives, qualitative genetics of major traits, breeding procedures as practiced in the field, markers and marker-assisted selection. genetic modification and varieties. Bt. cotton which has impacted cotton production scenario in India, global status of commercialized GM/biotech crops and MAS have been adequately covered in independent chapters. Relevant Indian legislations like Protection of Plant Varieties and Farmers'' Rights Act-2001 and Biodiversity Act-2002 figure prominently to expose the readers about these two legislations related to crop varieties IPR and effective PGR and biodiversity management. Landmark historical developments, namely, introduction of dwarfing genes in wheat and rice heralding Green Revolution in India have been adequately covered. Crop based national research centers/all India coordinated research projects and CGIAR funded crop improvement centers have been given due coverage to give a complete picture of individual crop breeding programme at one place. Any exciting development which has made an impact in the area of commercial crop breeding and biotechnology is available in this book which will be a rich source of information to undergraduate agriculture students and post-graduate students majoring in genetics, plant breeding, seed science and technology, and plant biotechnology and the professionals engaged in crop breeding. Show More'),
('Yoga Therapy, Ayurveda, and Western Medicine', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Yoga_Therapy_Ayurveda_and_Western_Medici-Dilip_Sarkar_-acf69-279890.jpg', 'Dilip Sarkar', 'Motilal Banarsidass Publishers (India)', NULL, '9789390696727', 'English', 424, NULL, 1390.0, 1390, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Writing a book is a time-consuming and-for me-daunting yet joyous endeavor. Like most authors, there are many people who supported me through this project and to whom I am extremely grateful. First, I would like to mention that I am very lucky to have a wonderful and talented family who encouraged me every step of the way through this project. I am particularly grateful to my wife, Shikha Sarkar, an accomplished visual and performing artist, who pushed me to get pen to paper. Using her amazing creative gifts, she helped design the front cover and the illustrations of this book. Through her continuous encouragement, I received the strength and discipline to stay up many late hours to distill and organize notes from the hundreds of talks and presentations I have done over the years into the basis for this book. Show More'),
('Competitive Mathematics', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Competitive_Mathematics-Dr_Banshidhar_Sahoo-206c6-269768.JPG', 'Dr. Banshidhar Sahoo', 'Techno World (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9789392145742', 'English', NULL, 'Edition, 2022', 1150.0, 1150, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '"Competitive Mathematics" is a resource designed for students preparing for competitive exams, focusing on building strong mathematical problem-solving skills. The book covers a wide range of topics essential for success in exams such as Olympiads, entrance tests, or aptitude-based assessments. It provides a comprehensive set of tools, tips, and strategies to tackle complex mathematical problems efficiently. Key features of the book include: Comprehensive Coverage: The book encompasses a wide variety of mathematical topics, including algebra, geometry, trigonometry, calculus, number theory, probability, and combinatorics. Each topic is explained with clarity, making it suitable for students at different levels of mathematical proficiency. Problem-Solving Techniques: One of the main focuses of the book is on problem-solving strategies. It provides step-by-step solutions to challenging problems, emphasizing different methods to approach and solve complex questions. This includes shortcuts, tricks, and techniques to optimize time and accuracy in competitive settings. Practice Problems: The book contains a large number of practice problems, ranging from basic to advanced levels. These problems help students develop their critical thinking and analytical skills, which are crucial in competitive exams. Solutions are often accompanied by explanations to help students understand the underlying concepts and methods. Exam-Oriented Approach: The structure of the book is tailored to the needs of competitive exam candidates. It presents problems in formats commonly seen in such exams, allowing students to familiarize themselves with the types of questions they are likely to encounter. Mock tests and previous exam questions are often included to provide realistic practice. Conceptual Clarity: The book emphasizes building a strong foundation in mathematical concepts, ensuring that students not only learn how to solve problems but also understand the principles behind them. This helps students adapt to different kinds of problems by applying core concepts flexibly. Logical and Analytical Skills Development: Beyond mathematics, the book enhances logical reasoning and analytical skills, essential for excelling in competitive exams. It trains students to approach problems with a clear and structured mindset, improving both speed and accuracy. Overall, "Competitive Mathematics" is a valuable resource for students aiming to excel in competitive examinations. It offers a combination of conceptual clarity, problem-solving strategies, and ample practice opportunities, helping learners build the confidence and skills needed to tackle even the toughest mathematical challenges. Show More'),
('Auditing: Principles And Practice', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/rokimg_20150705_59427.gif', 'Ravinder Kumar , Virender Sharma', 'Prentice Hall (India)', 'Department of Accounting', '9788120344723', 'English', 576, '2nd Edition, 2011', 5514.0, 5514, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Biogas Systems: Principles And Applications', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Biogas_Systems_Principles_And_Applicatio-KM_Mital-30430-278470.jpg', 'K.M. Mital', 'New Age International Publishers (India)', 'Agriculture', '9788122409475', 'English', 412, '1st published 1996', 1498.0, 1498, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Biogas can be produced by fermenting organic materials in absence of air (or oxygen) with the help of bacteria (micro-organisms) to break down materials to intermediates such as alcohols and fatty acids and finally to methane, carbon dioxide and water. This process is called anaerobic fermentation and was known to exist from quite long time back. Biogas has also been known as the swamp gas, sewer gas, fuel gas, marsh gas, wet gas, and in India more commonly as ''gobar'' gas. Natural gas is sis also produced by the action of anaerobic bacteria on plants that grew thousands of years ago. Biogas and natural gas are therefore very much akin to one another. The main fuel component of both is methane gas. However, over the years, pressure and temperature of underground rocks have converted part of the methane in natural gas to other gases such as ethane, propane, butane and the condensate. In contrast, biogas is produced in a digester by anaerobic fermentation. A period of 15 days or so enables anaerobic bacteria to convert organic matter to biogas which however is too short for the conversion of methane to other gases like ethane, propane, butane [35]. Show More'),
