('Comparative Materia Medica: 1', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Comparative_Materia_Medica_1-EA_Farrington-caa02-254051.jpg', 'E.A. Farrington', 'B.Jain Publishers (India)', 'Homeopathic', '9788131902110', 'English', 553, '1st Edition', 780.0, 780, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '"Comparative Materia Medica: 1" by S. R. Phatak is a detailed guide for homeopathic practitioners, focusing on the comparison of various homeopathic remedies based on their similarities and differences. The book is designed to help homeopaths fine-tune their remedy selection by highlighting subtle distinctions between remedies that may appear similar in their symptom profiles. Key elements of the book include: Remedy Comparisons: The primary aim of the book is to provide side-by-side comparisons of homeopathic remedies, making it easier for practitioners to differentiate between them. Remedies that share similar symptoms, modalities, or constitutional types are examined in depth, with Phatak drawing attention to their unique characteristics and differences. Practical Applications: The book is designed to be a practical tool for homeopathic case-taking. By offering comparisons between closely related remedies, it allows practitioners to refine their selections and choose the most appropriate remedy based on the patient’s specific needs and symptomology. Structure and Organization: Remedies are grouped and compared based on their major symptom categories, such as mental, emotional, and physical symptoms. This structured approach makes it easier for homeopaths to quickly find relevant information during clinical practice. Insights from Clinical Practice: Drawing from years of experience, Phatak offers clinical insights and observations that enhance the practical usefulness of the book. These insights help homeopaths understand how remedies perform in real-world cases, beyond what is found in standard Materia Medica texts. Enhanced Understanding: By offering a comparative approach, the book helps practitioners develop a deeper understanding of remedies. It encourages a more nuanced view of Materia Medica, emphasizing the importance of choosing remedies based not just on common symptoms but on the overall picture and constitution of the patient. Overall, "Comparative Materia Medica: 1" is a valuable resource for homeopaths who wish to improve their diagnostic accuracy by understanding the fine distinctions between similar remedies. It is particularly useful for students and experienced practitioners who want to enhance their prescribing skills and deepen their knowledge of homeopathic remedies. Show More'),
('Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Ordinary_and_Partial_Differential_Equati-Dr_M_D_Raisinghania-36cd5-332767.jpg', 'Dr. M. D. Raisinghania', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Department of Mathematics', '9789352836109', 'English', 912, '20th Edition, 2020', 1798.0, 1798, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This well-acclaimed book, now in its twentieth edition, continues to offer an in-depth presentation of the fundamental concepts and their applications of ordinary and partial differential equations providing systematic solution techniques. The book provides step-by-step proofs of theorems to enhance students'' problem-solving skill and includes plenty of carefully chosen solved examples to illustrate the concepts discussed. Designed as a textbook for undergraduate and postgraduate students of Mathematics and Physics as well as undergraduate students of all branches of Engineering and AMIE, this book would also be useful for the aspirants of GATE, CSIR-UGC (NET) and other competitive examinations. Show More'),
