('Thermodynamics', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Thermodynamics-Yunus_A_Cengel-fb5ec-328612.jpg', 'Yunus A. Cengel , Michael A. Boles , Mehmet Kanoglu', 'Mcgraw Hill Education (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9789353165741', 'English', 968, '9th Edition, 2019', 2250.0, 2250, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Distinguished as a best seller, the title Thermodynamics: An Engineering Approach is taking another step towards excellence with this revised edition. Through its careful explanations of concepts, and use of numerous practical examples and figures, this book aims to bridge the gap between knowledge and the confidence to properly apply it. Key Features:✔ Written in a self-instructive manner, it speaks to students, not over students✔ Emphasizes on the physical aspects of the subject matter in addition to mathematical representations and manipulations. ✔ Follows a physical, intuitive approach to help students master the practical problems✔ Contains a rich pool of pedagogy which revolve around the real-world problems Show More'),
('Aadhaar', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Aadhaar-Shankkar_Aiyar-578be-379573.jpg', 'Shankkar Aiyar', 'Harpercollins publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9789356993143', 'English', 256, 'Edition, 2024', 998.0, 998, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Aadhaar was born in July 2009, yoking modern technology and management expertise to political will. The biometric-based unique identification system, built by tech czar Nandan Nilekani and his team of innovators, was designed to enable subsidies and social spends reach their true destination, plug institutional corruption and save trillions of tax-rupees. In July 2017, Aadhaar is 1.15 billion identities and growing. In Aadhaar: A Biometric History of India''s 12-digit Revolution, senior journalist Shankkar Aiyar traces the history of this ambitious, controversial undertaking. He speaks with President Pranab Mukherjee, Prime Ministers Narendra Modi and Manmohan Singh, P. Chidambaram, Yashwant Sinha, Rahul Gandhi and others to document how politicians with diametrically opposed ideologies were equally determined to propel Aadhaar. Aiyar maps how Aadhaar''s application expanded beyond its original intent. He researches its ups, downs, and turnarounds; discusses the concerns of activists and bureaucrats on potential misuse of the database for state surveillance; raises the urgent need for a data-protection and privacy law and spells out the solutions. An unusual contemporary dramatization, this book is a breathless ride through recent changes in India''s political and economic landscape. Show More'),
('The USSR Olympiad Problem Book', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_USSR_Olympiad_Problem_Book-D_O_Shklarsky-b7c61-324316.jpg', 'D. O. Shklarsky', 'Dover Publications', 'Department of Mathematics', '978-0486277097', 'English', 780, 'Edition, 2003', 4950.0, 4950, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Product Deion Published by Dover Publications Inc., this ‘The USSR Olympiad Problem Book’ is a great choice for the students, who are preparing for the Olympiad examinations. Authored by D. O. Shklarsky, this book contains simple procedures for every complicated problem so that students find it easy to understand the concept involved in it. This book also includes selected theorems and problems of elementary mathematics. Salient Features of the Textbook • The problems are divided into twelve separate sections. • Students can brush up their mathematical skills on integers, evaluating sums and products, equations having integer solutions, complex numbers, miscellaneous algebraic problems and the algebra of polynomials. • Candidates can practice differences, sequences and sums and also problems of number theory. • Contains 320 unconventional problems for the students to practice. • The book covers trigonometry and also elementary number theory. • Comes with complete solutions to all problems. • Contains advanced problems with solutions in detail so that students are able to understand the concept involved in it. Show More'),
