('Corporate Accounting - Semester 3', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Corporate_Accounting-MC_Shukla-c3180-332227.jpg', 'M.C. Shukla , S. C. Gupta , T. C. Grewal', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Department of Accounting', '9789352836499', 'English', 816, NULL, 1198.0, 1198, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Corporate accounting has been especially written to meet the requirements of B.Com. Students as per the choice based Credit System (CBCS) curriculum of University of North Bengal. It comprehensively presents the fundamental concepts of corporate accounting in an informative and systematic manner. table of Contents: Chapter 1: Introduction Chapter 2: Issue and Forfeiture of shares Chapter 3: Issue and redemption of Debentures Chapter 4: Buy-back of shares and redemption of preference shares Chapter 5: Final Accounts of Joint stock company Chapter 6: Valuation of Goodwill Chapter 7: Valuation of shares Chapter 8: Cash Flow Statement Chapter 9: Amalgamation (combination) of Company and external reconstruction Chapter 10: Internal reconstruction of a Company Chapter 11: holding companies Chapter 12: Accounting Ratio. Show More'),
