('Introductory Mathematics For Engineering Applications', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Introductory_Mathematics_For_Engineering-Kuldip_Nayar-7a3ac-327761.jpg', 'Kuldip Nayar , S. S. Rattan', 'Wiley India Pvt. Ltd', 'Department of Mathematics', '9788126557479', 'English', 432, '1st Published, 2015', 1002.0, 1002, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Authors Rattan and Klingbeil have developed a new approach to engineering math that improves student motivation and success and supports greater retention of engineering majors. The book is designed specifically for engineering students, who specifically cite calculus as the reason for dropping out of engineering courses. Introduction to Engineering Math is designed to improve student retention, motivation and success through application-driven, just-in-time engineering math instruction provided by engineering faculty. Show More'),
('Engineering Physics', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Engineering_Physics-G_Vijayakumari-6f3b3-333807.jpg', 'G Vijayakumari', 'Vikas Publishing House (India)', 'Department of Physics and Applied Physics', '9789325982284', 'English', 340, '8th Edition, 2014', 598.0, 598, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Engineering Physics has been specifically designed and written to meet the requirements of the engineering students of GTU. All the topics and sub-topics are neatly arranged for the students. A number of assignment problems, along with questions and answers, have also been provided. MCQs for the bridge course have been designed in such a way that the students can recollect every concept that they have read and apply easily during the examination. Show More'),
('Principles of Education', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Principles_of_Education-_S_Venkateswaran-734a0-333340.jpg', 'S Venkateswaran', 'Vikas Publishing House (India)', 'Department of Education and Research', '9780706973440', 'English', 192, '1st Edition, 2018', 598.0, 598, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This book deals with the issues and trends in primary education in terms of curriculum construction, the agencies of education, the different schools of thought on education, and the role of schools and teachers. Care has been taken to include what education at this level should aim at and the duties of a teacher to achieve these aims. A brief note on great educators, their contribution to education and their educational experiments also form a part of this book. Show More'),
('Mathematics for B.Sc. Students -Algebra I and Calculus I', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Mathematics_for_BSc_Students_Algebra_I_a-Vanishree_R_K-5e5ce-332594.jpg', 'Vanishree R K', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Department of Mathematics', '9789355013668', 'English', 320, NULL, 598.0, 598, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This textbook has been conceptualized as per the recommended National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 and as per the syllabus prescribed by Karnataka State Higher Education Council (KSHEC) for B.Sc. students of Mathematics. It covers important topics such as Matrices, Polar Coordinates, Differential Calculus, Successive Differentiation, Number Theory, and Theory of Equations for sound conceptual understanding. Show More'),
('Physics For B.Sc. Students Semester V : Paper 1 - NEP 2020 - For the University of Uttar Pradesh', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Physics_For_BSc_Students_Semester_V__Pap-test_-7ad03-332495.jpg', 'Shubha A , C. L. Arora', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Department of Physics and Applied Physics', '9789355018281', 'English', 328, NULL, 598.0, 598, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This textbook has been specifically developed on the directives of National Education Policy (NEP 2020) and is as per latest curriculum of B. Sc. Physics (Fifth Semester) for the Universities of Uttar Pradesh. This book comprises of two parts: Part A and Part B. Part A deals with the Introduction of Classical Mechanics. This begins with Constrained Motion followed by Lagrangian Formalism, Hamiltonian Formalism and Motion under Central forces. Part B on Introduction of Statistical Mechanics starts with Macrostate and Microstate followed by Concept of Ensemble, Three Statistical Distribution Laws namely Maxwell-Boltzmann Statistics, Bose-Einstein Statistics and Fermi-Dirac Statistics. Their applications are lucidly explained at the end of the book. Show More'),
('Botany for B.Sc. Students', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Botany_for_BSc_Students-B_P_Pandey-f79b4-332391.jpg', 'B. P. Pandey', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Department of Botany', '9789355011275', 'English', 384, NULL, 598.0, 598, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This textbook has been designed to meet the needs of B.Sc. first semester students of Botany stream for universities of Karnataka as per the recommended National Education Policy (NEP) 2020. The book has been comprehensively written to provide full syllabus coverage with extensive details of concepts along with recent updates, illustrations, tables etc. The book has been written in lucid and easily understandable language for students. Each chapter has self-test exercise as well as a consolidated text on practical part along with viva voce questions at the end of the book. Show More'),
('Cost and Management Accounting', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/_Cost_and_Management_Accounting_-M_N_Arora-7d36c-332342.jpg', 'M N Arora , Priyanka Katyal', 'Vikas Publishing House (India)', 'Department of Accounting', '9789325980648', 'English', 524, NULL, 598.0, 598, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This book has been written specifically for the students of B. Com. (Hons.) of the Utkal University in accordance with its prescribed syllabus. It gives a through grounding in cost concepts, cost behavior and costing methods. Every discussion involving conceptual difficulties is immediately followed by a numerical example. Key Feature: - • Ideal for self-study, making learning a painless exercise. • Examination-oriented approach • Around 260 solved problems and illustrations accompanied by '';working notes'' • Theoretical, Practical and Objective Type Questions selected mostly from the past examinations Table of Content: - • Introduction • Accounting for Materials • Accounting for Labour (Employee Cost) • Overhead Cost • Output or Unit Costing (Cost Sheet) • Job Costing • Contract Costing • Process Costing • Marginal (Variable) Costing • Budgeting and Budgetary Control • Standard Costing and Variance Analysis Show More'),
