('Active Labor Market Policies in Europe', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Active_Labor_Market_Policies_in_Europe-Jochen_Kluve-ac042-301226.jpg', 'Jochen Kluve , David Card , Eleonora Patacchini', 'Springer (India)', 'Department of Education and Research', '9783540485575', 'English', 222, '1st published, 2007', 6948.0, 6948, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Quality Questioning', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Quality_Questioning-Beth_Dankert_Sattes-37aab-291155.jpg', 'Beth Dankert Sattes , Jackie A. Walsh', 'Corwin', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9781506328874', 'English', 264, '2nd Edition, 2016', 6862.0, 6862, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Foundation Mathematics For Computer Science: A Visual Approach', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Foundation_Mathematics_For_Computer_Scie-John_Vince-b67f8-328033.jpg', 'John Vince', 'Springer (India)', 'Department of Mathematics', '9783030420772', 'English', 407, '2nd Edition, 2020', 8472.0, 8472, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'In this second edition of Foundation Mathematics for Computer Science, John Vince has reviewed and edited the original book and written new chapters on combinatorics, probability, modular arithmetic and complex numbers. These subjects complement the existing chapters on number systems, algebra, logic, trigonometry, coordinate systems, determinants, vectors, matrices, geometric matrix transforms, differential and integral calculus. During this journey, the author touches upon more esoteric topics such as quaternions, octonions, Grassmann algebra, Barrycentric coordinates, transfinite sets and prime numbers. John Vince describes a range of mathematical topics to provide a solid foundation for an undergraduate course in computer science, starting with a review of number systems and their relevance to digital computers, and finishing with differential and integral calculus. Readers will find that the author’s visual approach will greatly improve their understanding as to why certain mathematical structures exist, together with how they are used in real-world applications. This second edition includes new, full-colour illustrations to clarify the mathematical descriptions, and in some cases, equations are also coloured to reveal vital algebraic patterns. The numerous worked examples will help consolidate the understanding of abstract mathematical concepts. Whether you intend to pursue a career in programming, scientific visualisation, artificial intelligence, systems design, or real-time computing, you should find the author’s literary style refreshingly lucid and engaging, and prepare you for more advanced texts. Show More'),
('Optimization and Nonstandard Analysis', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Optimization_and_Nonstandard_Analysis-J_E_Rubio-33b4b-322433.jpg', 'J. E. Rubio', 'CRC Press (India)', 'Department of Mathematics', '9780824792817', 'English', 376, '1st Edition, 1994', 8554.0, 8554, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Advanced Soil Mechanics', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Advanced_Soil_Mechanics-Braja_M_Das-d279e-328240.jpg', 'Braja M. Das', 'CRC Press (India)', 'Agriculture Engineering and Technology', '9780367730109', 'English', 734, '5th Edition, 2020', 8548.0, 8548, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Now in its fifth edition, this classic textbook continues to offer a well-tailored resource for beginning graduate students in geotechnical engineering. Further developing the basic concepts from undergraduate study, it provides a solid foundation for advanced study. This new edition addresses a variety of recent advances in the field and each section is updated. Braja Das particularly expands the content on consolidation, shear strength of soils, and both elastic and consolidation settlements of shallow foundations to accommodate modern developments. New material includes: Recently published correlations of maximum dry density and optimum moisture content of compaction Recent methods for determination of preconsolidation pressure A new correlation for recompression index Different approaches to estimating the degree of consolidation A discussion on the relevance of laboratory strength tests to field conditions Several new example problems This text can be followed by advanced courses dedicated to topics such as mechanical and chemical stabilization of soils, geo-environmental engineering, critical state soil mechanics, geosynthetics, rock mechanics, and earthquake engineering. It can also be used as a reference by practical consultants. Show More'),
('Introductory Mathematics For Engineering Applications', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Introductory_Mathematics_For_Engineering-Kuldip_S_Rattan-a3190-327776.jpg', 'Kuldip S. Rattan , Nathan W. Klingbeil', 'Wiley India Pvt. Ltd', 'Department of Mathematics', '9781118466162', 'English', 460, '2nd Edition, 2012', 7346.0, 7346, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Rattan and Klingbeil’s Introductory Mathematics for Engineering Applications is designed to help improve engineering student retention and success through application-driven, just-in-time engineering math instruction. It is intended to be taught by engineering faculty, not math faculty, so the emphasis is on using math to solve engineering problems, not on derivations and theory. The book is a product of several major grants to develop and disseminate a new approach to engineering mathematics education. The authors have developed a course that does just this, and faculty at more than two dozen institutions have piloted aspects of this course in their own curricula. This approach covers only the salient math topics actually used in core engineering courses, including physics, statics, dynamics, electric circuits and computer programming. More importantly, the course replaces traditional math prerequisites for the above core courses, so that students can advance in the engineering curriculum without first completing the required calculus sequence. The result has shifted the traditional emphasis on math prerequisite requirements to an emphasis on engineering motivation for math, and has had an overwhelming impact on engineering student retention. Show More'),
('Educating Individuals With Disabilities', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Educating_Individuals_With_Disabilities-Elena_L_Grigorenko-c7920-330605.jpg', NULL, 'Springer Publishing Co Inc', 'Foreign Language Books: Professional, Journal and Reference', '9780826103567', 'English', 512, '1st Edition, 2008', 7512.0, 7512, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Advances in Botanical Research', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Advances_in_Botanical_Research_-J_A_Callow-ceb62-291939.jpg', 'J. A. Callow', 'Academic Press, India', 'Agriculture', '9780120059430', 'English', 304, '1st published 2006', 7022.0, 7022, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('The Making Of Neo-Liberal India: Nationalism, Gender And The Paradoxes Of Globalisation', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Making_Of_Neo_Liberal_India_National-Rupal_Oza-58a6e-311263.jpg', 'Rupal Oza', 'Women Unlimited', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '8188965286', 'English', 208, '1st published, 2006', 600.0, 600, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This book examines the impact of globalisation on the discourse on Indian culture and identity. Though concerned primarily with developments following the liberalisation of the economy in the early 1990s, an extended history is provided of each of the issues addressed, which reveals the gradual mutations in definitions of ‘women’s liberation’ or ‘national security.’ Three sites of public debate are explored — the introduction of satellite television and the opening up of the airwaves; the 1996 Miss World pageant; and India’s declaration of nuclear weapons capability in 1998. Drawing on sources ranging from court cases to commercial advertising, the author tracks the efforts to realign the borders and boundaries of the nation-state through the rhetoric of safeguarding sexual mores and of masculine virility. Show More'),
('STOP Assuming', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/book_av.png', 'Bob Schoenberg', 'Heuristic Books', 'Foreign Language Books: Business, Investment and Economics', '9781596301054', 'English', 144, 'Edition, 2017', 3384.0, 3384, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'In this book, Bob Schoenberg, a recognized teacher and trainer of critical thinking skills and an expert in the Designed Change Process, provides a simple yet highly effective way to help you stop assuming.Personal assumptions can greatly influence what you think, what you say and even what you do. They tend to be hidden, negative or restrictive. Once you stop assuming, you can begin to make significant positive changes in your life. To Stop Assuming follow these three steps:1)Identify your personal assumption.2)Use the "Special Roleplay" to challenge it.3)Use Enhancement techniques to strengthen those skills, talents or traits that you feel are weak or lacking.Here are the author''s thoughts about the materials he developed: When I first used this process on myself I was blown away by how effective it is. Suddenly, I saw all sorts of possibilities I had never seen before. It was like opening a door that I never even knew existed that contained all sorts of possibilities - Bob Schoenberg Show More'),
