('Analytical Methods in Soil Science and Agricultural Chemistry', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Analytical_Methods_in_Soil_Science_and_A-Shivanna_M-1101a-372952.jpg', 'Shivanna M.', 'Kalyani Publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: University', '9789355408525', 'English', 380, '1st Edition, 2023', 790.0, 790, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This book "Analytical Methods in Soil Science and Agricultural Chemistry" is a compilation of some user-friendly analytical methods for characterizing soil physical, chemical and biological properties as well as determining nutrient content of plant in a very lucid manner. The book not only describes the analytical methods in detail but discusses the basic principle of the analysis as well as the relevant queries and their solution for the benefit of all users, particularly students. The book has also discussed the principle of functioning of different analytical instruments used in soil and plant analysis and some easy understanding basic concepts of different analytical methods. The book will be useful to students at agricultural universities/institutes, scientists/technicians engaged in soil analysis laboratories. The book has been written in a simple language and understandable manner. The contents of the book include 18 chapters. All chapters should be thoroughly viewed as a concise collection of various topics from different books, journals, bulletins, research articals and research papers etc. Figures and tables have also been provided wherever necessary. It is hoped that this textbook will help to improve the knowledge of students regarding plant nutrients and their analysis. All suggestions and criticisms for further improvement of this book will be thankfully acknowledged. Show More'),
('Inderbir Singh''s Human Embryology', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Inderbir_Singhs_Human_Embryology-Devi_V_Subhadra-2ad11-308940.jpg', 'Devi V Subhadra', 'Jaypee Brothers Medical Publisher (India)', 'Embryology', '9789354658860', 'English', 370, '13th Edition, 2023', 1900.0, 1900, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '-Cell potency: Potential to differentiate into different cell types. -Development: A process where something grows or changes and becomes more advanced. -Differentiation: Qualitative change in structure for an assigned function. -Embryo: Developing individual during the first two months or eight weeks of intrauterine life (IUL). Embryo (G): (en = with in; bruein = to swell or to be full); Logos = study. -Embryology: Study of development of an individual before birth. -Fertilization: Process of fusion of male and female gametes. It takes place in the uterine tube of female genital tract. -Fetus: Developing individual from 3rd month or 9th week of intrauterine life to time of birth. -Gametogenesis: This is the process of production of gametes in gonads or sex organs. In males it is known as spermatogenesis and in females as oogenesis. Show More'),
('Refresher Course in Physics Volume -III', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Refresher_Course_in_Physics_Volume_III-C_L_Arora-94dca-332500.jpg', 'C. L. Arora', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Department of Physics and Applied Physics', '9789355010865', 'English', 944, NULL, 1050.0, 1050, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Refresher Course in Physics Volume -III, Section-I: Solid State Physics: 1. Crystal Structure, 2. Crystal Diffraction and Reciprocal Lattice, 3. Crystal Bonding, 4. Lattice Vibrations, 5. Free Electron Theory of Metals, 6. Band Theory of Solids, 7. Semiconductors, 8. Super Conductivity, 9. Magnetic and Dielectric Properties, Section-II: Electronics: 1. Semi-Conductor Diodes, 2. Rectifiers and Filters, 3. Bipolar Junction Transistors, 4. Field Effect Transistor, 5. Transistor Biasing, 6. Feedback Amplifiers, 7. Oscillators, 8. Modulation and Detection, 9. Radio Communication, 10. Cathode Ray Oscillograph and Television, 11. Valve Electronics, 12. Network Theorems, Section-III: Nuclear And Particle Physics: 1. Atomic Nucleus, Nuclear Models, 3. Radioactivity, 4. Nuclear Reactions and Fissions, 5. Interaction of Nuclear Radiation with Matter, 6. Particle Accelerators, 7. Radiation Detectors, 8. Cosmic Rays and Elementary Particles Show More'),
('Corporate Accounting-Semester 3', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Corporate_Accounting-MC_Shukla-0b2cc-332225.jpg', 'M.C. Shukla , S. C. Gupta , T. C. Grewal', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Department of Accounting', '978-9352836475', 'English', 184, NULL, 998.0, 998, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Corporate accounting has been especially written to meet the requirements of B.Com. Students as per the choice based Credit System (CBCS) curriculum of Bangalore University. It comprehensively presents the fundamental concepts of corporate accounting in an informative and systematic manner. table of Contents: Chapter 1: underwriting of shares and Debentures Chapter 2: Profit or loss prior to incorporation Chapter 3: Valuation of Goodwill Chapter 4: Valuation of shares Chapter 5: Final Accounts of Joint stock company. Show More'),
('Physics For B.Sc. Students Semester IV - NEP 2020 Uttar Pradesh', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Physics_For_BSc_Students_Semester_IV-test_-7be50-332498.jpg', 'Shubha A , C. L. Arora', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Department of Physics and Applied Physics', '9789355017017', 'English', 344, NULL, 698.0, 698, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'This book has been conceptualized as per the recommended National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 and as per syllabus prescribed by Universities of Uttar Pradesh for B. Sc. Students of Physics for the Fourth Semester. This textbook comprehensively covers two papers: Theory and Practical. Part A begins with Structure of Space-Time in Newtonian Mechanics, Galilean Transformation and Electromagnetism Leading to the Foundation of Theory of Relativity is studied in detail. The experimental background of Michelson-Morley Experiment and its Significance of Discarding the Existence of either developed the relativistic kinematics. Inadequacies of Classical Mechanics, Black Body Radiation, Max-Planck''s Quantum Hypothesis and Concept of Matter Waves are elaborately explained in a simple manner. Part B deals with the electronics branch which covers transistor biasing, amplifiers, feedback, and oscillator circuits are lucidly explained with suitable examples. Show More'),
