('Practical Biotechnology and Plant Tissue Culture', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Practical_Biotechnology_and_Plant_Tissue-Santosh_Nagar-3ee23-333296.jpg', 'Santosh Nagar , Madhavi Adhav', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Agriculture TK. 398', '9788121932004', 'English', 121, '1st Edition, 2010', 398.0, 398, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '• The book starts with an introduction to basic knowledge of instruments which deals with principle, working, uses, limitations and precautions of about ten instruments.Basic Knowledge of precaution of;Culture Media for Bacterial Growth, Plant Tissue Culture and Standard Solutions has been given in simple and easy-to-follow language. • The biotechnology exercises such as Plasmid and DNA isolation, DNA size determination, Restriction digestion, PCR, Gus gene assay, RFLP, RAPD, Isolation of bacteria by streak and Pour plate method, Growth characteristics of E.Coli by Plating and Turbidimetric method and the plant tissues culture exercises such as Cell suspension culture, Androgenesis, Somatic embryogenesis, Preparation of plantlet to greenhouse field, have been given in a student friendly manner. • Matter for Viva-voce has also been included. Show More'),
('Basic Surgical Skills And Techniques', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Basic_Surgical_Skills_And_Techniques-_Sudhir_Kumar_Jain-f09d4-250857.jpg', 'Sudhir Kumar Jain , David L Stoker , Raman Tanwar', 'Jaypee Brothers Medical Publisher (India)', 'Surgery', '9789386322814', 'English', 210, '3rd Edition, 2018', 2300.0, 2300, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Salient Features • Focuses on the basic art of surgery Reflects not only the success of basic surgical skills and techniques but brings also the latest advances in surgery to the readers • Adds the information on robotic surgery, newer LASERS, instruments and common surgical operations along with revision of each and every chapter Embraces the basic principles of surgery and explains the details in a lucid manner Written by the authors who have been awarded globally for their academic excellence Illustrated with lucid diagrams and studded with many surgical pearls Useful for students studying the art and science of surgery everywhere. Show More'),
('Textbook Of Veterinary Microbiology', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Textbook_Of_Veterinary_Microbiology-S_N_SHARMA-23aaa-332481.jpg', 'S. N. SHARMA , S. C. ADLAKHA', 'Vikas Publishing House (India)', 'Veterinary and Animal Husbandry TK. 998', '9788125900399', 'English', 420, NULL, 998.0, 998, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'The Textbook of Veterinary Microbiology is specially designed to meet the requirements of Veterinary and Animal Science Students of the developing countries of Asia, Africa and Latin America. The book provides general background of Veterinary Microbiology with special reference to infectious diseases of livestock. The first part of the book covers microbial biology, covering the history and scope of veterinary microbiology, general characters and classification of viruses, bacteria and fungi. In the second part, bacterial pathogens and associated diseases of animals and poultry have been covered with emphasis on diagnosis and control of important diseases. In the third part, information on pathogenic viruses and associated diseases of livestock has been provided with special reference to diagnostic and preventive aspects. In the fourth part, pathogenic fungi and the animal diseases caused by them have been described. Micro-organisms of little or no pathogenic importance have been omitted while greater emphasis has been placed on micro-organisms causing diseases which result in severe economic losses in the developing countries of Asia, Africa and Latin America. This book has been prepared according to the syllabus approved by the Veterinary Council of India and would fulfill the needs of veterinary students in the discipline of microbiology. The veterinary disease investigators and the practitioners of veterinary medicine also will find the book useful for reference and guidance. Show More'),
('Veterinary Surgical Techniques', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Veterinary_Surgical_Techniques-_Amresh_Kumar_-fdc30-334336.jpg', 'Amresh Kumar', 'S Chand Publishing (India)', 'Veterinary and Animal Husbandry 1 Rating  | No Review TK. 1,198', '9788125902447', 'English', 416, 'Edition, 2020', 1198.0, 1198, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'The majority of surgical procedures in large animals especially in cattle and buffaloes can be done safely and painlessly with some form of physical restraint and regional and local anaesthesia. In small animals, majority of operations would require the use of general anaesthesia. The restraint can either be achieved by use of simple means like nose twitch, nose-lead, elevating the tail over the back, use of chute etc. in large animals and tape muzzle in small animals or by use of sedatives and tranquilizers. For effective physical restraint in large or small animals, the clinician should be quite familiar with the commonly used knots. Restraint achieved with tranquilizers and sedatives usually minimizes the amount of physical restraint and would also facilitate administration of general anaesthesia and reduce their dosage. Show More'),
